cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ForgeLM in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "ForgeLM"
abstract: >-
  Config-driven LLM fine-tuning: validated YAML in, a fine-tuned model and an
  evidence trail out. Covers SFT, DPO, SimPO, KTO, ORPO and GRPO, with optional
  dataset auditing, safety evaluation, evaluation gates, human approval and
  EU AI Act compliance artifacts. The same configuration runs from a terminal,
  a notebook, or a CI/CD pipeline.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ForgeLM Contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/HodeTech/ForgeLM"
url: "https://hodetech.github.io/ForgeLM/"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - llm
  - fine-tuning
  - lora
  - qlora
  - peft
  - trl
  - dpo
  - grpo
  - reproducibility
  - mlops
  - eu-ai-act
  - ai-governance
# `version` and `date-released` are intentionally omitted. They would be a
# second copy of the release version, which `forgelm/_version.py`, `pyproject.toml`
# and CHANGELOG.md already carry, and nothing would keep the copies in sync.
# Add them together with a release-checklist step (or a guard) if citations
# need to name a specific release.
